WEBVTT

00:00:08.080 --> 00:00:10.270
We're one week away from the school festival.

00:00:10.900 --> 00:00:14.730
A new board game café opened near our school.

00:00:15.330 --> 00:00:19.820
We decided to pay a visit, to see if we
could learn something for our festival...

00:00:20.870 --> 00:00:21.700
This must be the place.

00:00:23.410 --> 00:00:24.700
Café Geschenk.

00:00:24.700 --> 00:00:26.240
Seems like it.

00:00:28.120 --> 00:00:29.500
Hello.

00:00:32.080 --> 00:00:33.750
There's nobody here.

00:00:33.750 --> 00:00:36.880
That's odd. Maybe they're not open yet.

00:00:39.040 --> 00:00:40.880
No, there's someone there!

00:00:45.830 --> 00:00:47.020
Is she asleep...?

00:00:47.020 --> 00:00:48.680
Does she work here?

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:56.020
Welcome...

00:00:57.540 --> 00:01:00.610
She's so pretty! She's from overseas!

00:01:02.700 --> 00:01:05.450
Hello, nice to meet you, we are--

00:01:05.450 --> 00:01:07.200
This isn't the first time we've met.

00:01:08.450 --> 00:01:10.790
Nice to re-meet you!

00:02:43.670 --> 00:02:46.370
You passed by us on the street?!

00:02:46.370 --> 00:02:52.700
Yes, that's how I know you.
You were talking about board games.

00:02:52.700 --> 00:02:54.830
What kind of coincidence is this...?

00:02:54.830 --> 00:02:56.600
Really... I'm surprised.

00:02:56.600 --> 00:03:01.110
My name is Emilia. Call me Emmy please.

00:03:01.110 --> 00:03:04.040
I'm Takayashiki Aya! Just Aya is fine!

00:03:04.040 --> 00:03:05.410
I'm Ono Midori.

00:03:05.410 --> 00:03:07.200
I'm Takekasa Miki.

00:03:07.200 --> 00:03:09.160
Great to see you all!

00:03:09.410 --> 00:03:11.740
Emmy, where are you from?

00:03:12.040 --> 00:03:13.700
From Hamburg, Germany.

00:03:13.700 --> 00:03:16.830
Oh, a major center of board
game culture! I'm jealous.

00:03:16.830 --> 00:03:21.250
Yes. In Germany, kids and adults all play games.

00:03:21.250 --> 00:03:24.050
But in Japan, there aren't
as many places to play games.

00:03:24.370 --> 00:03:26.450
So we opened this shop.

00:03:26.450 --> 00:03:28.760
Huh? This is your own shop?

00:03:28.760 --> 00:03:31.970
No, my dad is the one who opened the shop.

00:03:32.910 --> 00:03:34.640
Um, thank you for your hospitality...

00:03:34.640 --> 00:03:36.310
Welcome.

00:03:37.160 --> 00:03:40.560
I'm here to help my dad.

00:03:41.160 --> 00:03:42.950
What a huge selection of games...!

00:03:42.950 --> 00:03:46.610
Yes, and it covers everything from
kids' games to core gamer favorites...

00:03:46.660 --> 00:03:49.750
Emmy's father really knows his stuff.

00:03:49.750 --> 00:03:54.950
Please choose any game you like.
If you don't know the rules, I will explain.

00:03:54.950 --> 00:03:58.790
What? Just explain? Let's play together!

00:03:58.790 --> 00:04:01.630
Really? Can I play with you?

00:04:01.630 --> 00:04:04.450
Of course! It would be more fun that way.

00:04:04.450 --> 00:04:05.340
Yes.

00:04:07.870 --> 00:04:09.870
Wh-What's wrong, Emmy?!

00:04:09.870 --> 00:04:16.700
This is the first time I'll play games
with girls my age in Japan...

00:04:16.700 --> 00:04:20.690
Danke schön! (Thank you!)
 Aya-san, Midori-san, Miki-san!

00:04:21.160 --> 00:04:23.440
So cute!

00:04:24.540 --> 00:04:25.500
<i>Keltis!</i>

00:04:25.500 --> 00:04:28.660
Yes! This is my favorite game.

00:04:28.660 --> 00:04:30.570
Nice. I like this one, too.

00:04:30.910 --> 00:04:32.370
The board is so pretty!

00:04:32.370 --> 00:04:35.000
Seriously! And these fantastic patterns...

00:04:35.000 --> 00:04:37.750
This pattern is called a Celtic knot.

00:04:37.750 --> 00:04:38.660
Celtic...?

00:04:38.660 --> 00:04:42.380
The Celts were a European
civilization from the BC era.

00:04:42.660 --> 00:04:46.550
The Celtic Knots are patterns that they made.

00:04:46.830 --> 00:04:51.080
They say modern-day Ireland
was built by the Celts, right?

00:04:51.080 --> 00:04:54.300
Yes! My mom is Irish.

00:04:54.300 --> 00:04:55.720
Wow!

00:04:56.330 --> 00:04:56.970
Hmm?

00:04:57.290 --> 00:04:58.870
That necklace...

00:04:58.870 --> 00:05:01.230
Yes! This is a Celtic charm.

00:05:01.620 --> 00:05:06.980
My mom gave it to me.
It has the power to make wishes come true.

00:05:08.000 --> 00:05:08.950
So pretty!

00:05:08.950 --> 00:05:10.290
Yes, really.

00:05:12.540 --> 00:05:14.620
Okay, here are the rules.

00:05:14.620 --> 00:05:18.540
You start with eight cards and five pieces.

00:05:18.540 --> 00:05:20.830
Wow, the cards are pretty, too!

00:05:20.830 --> 00:05:22.960
The pieces are cute, too! A clover!

00:05:23.250 --> 00:05:25.290
There are five card colors.

00:05:25.580 --> 00:05:28.300
On your turn, you play a card.

00:05:28.300 --> 00:05:32.340
You put a piece on the path with the
same color as the card you played.

00:05:33.120 --> 00:05:36.750
The cards have a number, zero to ten.

00:05:36.750 --> 00:05:40.120
Your first card can be any number.

00:05:40.120 --> 00:05:44.330
But when you play your second card,
it determines what you can play after that.

00:05:44.330 --> 00:05:45.160
Huh?

00:05:45.160 --> 00:05:49.450
Like this. You play cards with
the same color on top of each other.

00:05:49.450 --> 00:05:51.950
I played a four, then a six.

00:05:51.950 --> 00:05:57.790
After that, I can only play a six or greater.

00:05:57.790 --> 00:06:04.910
If I had played the six before the four,
then I could only play four or smaller.

00:06:04.910 --> 00:06:10.410
I see! Cards of the same color
can only go up or down in number!

00:06:10.410 --> 00:06:12.000
Exactly!

00:06:12.000 --> 00:06:18.790
When you play a card, the piece on the
path with that color advances one space.

00:06:18.790 --> 00:06:22.950
There are five paths, and there
can be only one piece per path.

00:06:22.950 --> 00:06:25.330
You can go down all five paths if you want.

00:06:25.330 --> 00:06:30.370
But the first three spaces give you
a negative score, so watch out!

00:06:30.370 --> 00:06:32.910
I see, it says negative.

00:06:32.910 --> 00:06:37.750
At the end of the game, you get points
depending on where your pieces are.

00:06:37.750 --> 00:06:39.120
So...

00:06:39.120 --> 00:06:42.500
I have to play at least four
cards to not go negative...

00:06:42.500 --> 00:06:47.250
Also, you have one big piece.
This one gets double the score.

00:06:47.250 --> 00:06:48.540
I see...

00:06:48.540 --> 00:06:52.500
But it also doubles the negative,
so you have to be careful with it.

00:06:52.500 --> 00:06:53.750
Oh...

00:06:53.750 --> 00:06:57.080
There are three types of tiles on the path.

00:06:57.080 --> 00:07:02.790
Numbered tiles give you points.
You get points equal to the number.

00:07:02.790 --> 00:07:05.120
The clover tile is a One More.

00:07:05.120 --> 00:07:08.330
If you land on this tile, you can move again.

00:07:08.330 --> 00:07:11.950
In that case, you can move
a different piece instead, right?

00:07:11.950 --> 00:07:17.250
Yes, exactly! If you use it well,
you can move many spaces at once.

00:07:17.250 --> 00:07:19.870
This is a very important rule.

00:07:21.450 --> 00:07:26.290
The third type is the Wishing Stone.
There are nine total.

00:07:26.290 --> 00:07:32.080
This tile is first come, first serve.
The person to land there first gets the stone.

00:07:32.080 --> 00:07:37.910
Collecting stones gives you points,
but you need at least two or you lose points.

00:07:37.910 --> 00:07:39.450
Another negative score?!

00:07:39.450 --> 00:07:45.950
I see, you have to have at least two to get
any points. Negative four for zero stones?!

00:07:45.950 --> 00:07:48.950
The area of the board with the
darker green is the goal zone.

00:07:48.950 --> 00:07:54.410
The game ends when a total
of five pieces enter the goal zone.

00:07:54.410 --> 00:07:57.540
That's all for the rules. Everyone okay?

00:07:57.540 --> 00:07:59.330
Yes! I think so!

00:07:59.330 --> 00:08:01.870
Let's get started then!

00:08:01.870 --> 00:08:03.450
Yes!

00:08:03.790 --> 00:08:07.120
The player who's been to Ireland
the most recently goes first!

00:08:07.120 --> 00:08:07.950
Huh?

00:08:07.950 --> 00:08:12.500
I see, you're playing with
the Celtic theme. But...

00:08:12.500 --> 00:08:15.450
Yes! I went last year!

00:08:15.450 --> 00:08:18.120
Wait, are you kidding?! Is that even fair?!

00:08:18.120 --> 00:08:21.540
It's kind of a cliché joke.

00:08:21.540 --> 00:08:24.080
So I will go first!

00:08:24.080 --> 00:08:25.580
Yellow, ten!

00:08:25.580 --> 00:08:28.910
I will drop my big piece!

00:08:28.910 --> 00:08:30.450
The big piece, right away...?

00:08:30.450 --> 00:08:32.330
Okay, I will do the big piece, too.

00:08:32.330 --> 00:08:33.690
Midori-chan, too?!

00:08:33.790 --> 00:08:39.000
If I have many cards of one color,
I know there's a high chance I can get far.

00:08:39.000 --> 00:08:40.950
I see...

00:08:40.950 --> 00:08:46.450
My colors are all mixed... I'll just play
it safe with the small piece for now.

00:08:46.450 --> 00:08:48.080
Me, too.

00:08:55.120 --> 00:08:58.580
What? How?! I can't play anymore!

00:08:58.580 --> 00:09:00.830
I can't play the red nine anymore,

00:09:00.830 --> 00:09:04.620
and the others would stop me from
moving much further beyond that...

00:09:04.620 --> 00:09:08.620
In those situations, you can discard
a card and draw another from the deck.

00:09:08.620 --> 00:09:09.790
Really?!

00:09:09.790 --> 00:09:13.500
However, the card you discarded
can be picked up by any other player.

00:09:13.500 --> 00:09:15.790
So you want to throw away
the card that nobody else wants.

00:09:15.790 --> 00:09:16.620
Huh...

00:09:16.620 --> 00:09:19.250
Cards that nobody wants...?

00:09:19.250 --> 00:09:24.500
Aya-san, try to look at what other
people have played, not what you have.

00:09:24.500 --> 00:09:29.330
For example, a person who has
played blue nine, seven, and six

00:09:29.330 --> 00:09:32.370
won't take any blue cards greater than seven.

00:09:32.370 --> 00:09:34.370
So in that case...

00:09:36.500 --> 00:09:37.540
I get it!

00:09:37.540 --> 00:09:38.580
This one!

00:09:38.580 --> 00:09:41.700
Yes! Nobody wants that one.

00:09:41.700 --> 00:09:43.700
Thanks, Emmy!

00:09:43.700 --> 00:09:45.870
Now it's my turn.

00:09:45.870 --> 00:09:49.250
I play a green three, get one point.

00:09:49.250 --> 00:09:53.330
Land on a clover, move this
other piece, two points.

00:09:53.330 --> 00:09:58.040
I landed on another clover,
so move this other piece...

00:09:58.040 --> 00:10:00.040
Total of three points!

00:10:00.040 --> 00:10:03.500
Wow! You moved three pieces in one go!

00:10:03.500 --> 00:10:06.000
I've never lost in this game.

00:10:06.000 --> 00:10:09.660
A clover chain... She is as good as she says.

00:10:09.660 --> 00:10:13.120
But I don't think I need to be too alarmed yet.

00:10:13.120 --> 00:10:15.000
One point here.

00:10:15.000 --> 00:10:17.330
Two points here.

00:10:17.330 --> 00:10:19.330
Midori-chan got three points, too!

00:10:20.620 --> 00:10:25.750
Okay, I play this green four, then move this one...

00:10:25.750 --> 00:10:27.120
And this one...

00:10:27.120 --> 00:10:28.540
And this one!

00:10:28.540 --> 00:10:31.580
Miki-chan got a clover chain going, too?!

00:10:31.580 --> 00:10:33.000
This is fun!

00:10:33.000 --> 00:10:36.410
Yes, when you get the chains
going, it feels really good.

00:10:37.410 --> 00:10:39.290
What's wrong, Emmy?

00:10:39.290 --> 00:10:41.370
I'm so happy right now.

00:10:41.370 --> 00:10:42.200
Huh?

00:10:42.200 --> 00:10:45.040
Japanese people like cute things, yes?

00:10:45.040 --> 00:10:47.750
I love cute things, too!

00:10:47.750 --> 00:10:51.160
So I'm happy to be able
to play games with cute girls!

00:10:51.160 --> 00:10:52.000
Huh?!

00:10:52.000 --> 00:10:52.660
C...

00:10:52.660 --> 00:10:53.660
Cute?!

00:10:53.660 --> 00:10:56.580
Thank you! You're super cute, too, Emmy!

00:10:58.750 --> 00:11:04.160
Am I somehow feeling the
same vibes from these two...?

00:11:05.660 --> 00:11:08.750
I'll play a blue one...

00:11:08.750 --> 00:11:14.580
Now, if one more piece enters
the goal zone, the game is over.

00:11:14.580 --> 00:11:19.250
What?! It's over already?! I still have
three pieces in the negative area!

00:11:19.250 --> 00:11:26.080
Aya, you've played all your pieces.
You need to focus on a few to get far.

00:11:26.080 --> 00:11:30.450
Ugh, at the very least I'll move
my big piece one space...

00:11:30.450 --> 00:11:31.910
Me, too...

00:11:33.700 --> 00:11:37.370
Okay! Now the game is over.

00:11:38.830 --> 00:11:41.040
Let's tally up the score!

00:11:42.450 --> 00:11:47.080
I got 31 points. Midori-san...

00:11:48.200 --> 00:11:50.620
Thirty-four points...?

00:11:50.620 --> 00:11:57.040
I... lost?! I don't believe it...
I lost in <i>Keltis</i>...

00:11:57.040 --> 00:11:58.830
Hey, Emmy?!

00:11:59.870 --> 00:12:03.870
I'm so impressed!
You're the first person to beat me!

00:12:03.870 --> 00:12:04.980
Huh?

00:12:04.980 --> 00:12:07.490
She's happy that she lost?

00:12:04.980 --> 00:12:07.490
So impressive! Super!

00:12:09.120 --> 00:12:12.750
I have so many negatives.
I have only 12 points...

00:12:12.750 --> 00:12:14.870
For your first time, it's not bad.

00:12:15.450 --> 00:12:16.580
Emmy...

00:12:16.580 --> 00:12:19.580
You'll do better next time!

00:12:19.580 --> 00:12:20.790
Emmy...!

00:12:22.330 --> 00:12:24.290
There, there.

00:12:24.290 --> 00:12:25.370
Midori-chan.

00:12:25.370 --> 00:12:27.000
Hmm? What is it?

00:12:27.000 --> 00:12:31.120
Let's hope the School
Festival Café is this exciting.

00:12:32.160 --> 00:12:34.200
School Festival?

00:12:34.200 --> 00:12:40.140
Our high school is having a festival soon.
We're going to do a board game café!

00:12:40.140 --> 00:12:44.110
Oh! How nice! I love festivals.

00:12:44.290 --> 00:12:48.620
By the way, your uniform... Is your school...?

00:12:48.620 --> 00:12:52.000
It's Kamogawa North High School, very close by.

00:12:52.000 --> 00:12:57.040
Oh, I just transferred there.
I'm starting in September.

00:12:57.040 --> 00:12:59.410
Wait, so you're in our school?!

00:13:00.870 --> 00:13:06.960
My mom was right. My wish came true.

00:13:07.250 --> 00:13:08.550
Your wish?

00:13:08.550 --> 00:13:13.510
I wished that I could see the girls
I walked by the other day again...

00:13:13.510 --> 00:13:18.810
And I wished to become friends with them
so I could play games with them!

00:13:26.700 --> 00:13:29.400
The day of the festival has arrived.

00:13:30.250 --> 00:13:32.660
Some students worked in food
stalls to raise the excitement.

00:13:33.040 --> 00:13:35.160
Some performed on a stage to
let their youthful passions explode.

00:13:35.950 --> 00:13:37.450
And...

00:13:37.450 --> 00:13:39.410
Nobody's coming.

00:13:39.410 --> 00:13:40.250
Yeah...

00:13:40.250 --> 00:13:45.710
It must be her. I didn't think she
would back down so easily, but...

00:13:46.130 --> 00:13:47.960
Second floor of the old building?

00:13:48.450 --> 00:13:50.700
Why did you put them so far out of the way?

00:13:50.700 --> 00:13:54.050
Their application was very late,
and that was the only venue left.

00:13:54.050 --> 00:13:59.200
That's a waste.
The project seemed so interesting.

00:13:59.200 --> 00:14:02.560
We don't need that to succeed!

00:14:04.120 --> 00:14:06.330
After all the effort we put in!

00:14:06.330 --> 00:14:08.500
What should we do, Midori-<i>chan</i>...?

00:14:09.540 --> 00:14:13.070
We have to do something to let
people know that we're out here...

00:14:15.160 --> 00:14:16.830
I finally found you!

00:14:16.830 --> 00:14:18.290
Emmy!

00:14:18.290 --> 00:14:19.540
<i>Guten morgen! (Good morning!)</i>

00:14:19.700 --> 00:14:21.910
You came! Thank you!

00:14:21.910 --> 00:14:28.120
Yes! I had to search a lot! Why did you
put yourself in such a remote location?

00:14:29.370 --> 00:14:35.580
I know, right? The whole festival might
be over by the time we get a customer...

00:14:35.580 --> 00:14:37.160
Don't worry, Aya!

00:14:37.160 --> 00:14:38.080
Huh?

00:14:38.080 --> 00:14:40.750
I brought something nice!

00:14:40.750 --> 00:14:41.950
Hmm...?

00:14:43.000 --> 00:14:45.870
Where's the board game café...? What?!

00:14:45.870 --> 00:14:47.870
Second floor of the old building?!

00:14:47.870 --> 00:14:50.160
Yoshioka-<i>kun</i>! So hot!

00:14:50.160 --> 00:14:51.790
Look over here, please!

00:14:51.790 --> 00:14:53.950
Hey, it's Ryuji.

00:14:53.950 --> 00:14:56.000
Popular with the girls, as always...

00:14:56.000 --> 00:14:58.830
He's just a kendo nut.

00:14:58.830 --> 00:15:00.540
Hey, Shouta!

00:15:01.620 --> 00:15:03.790
Why are you following me around?

00:15:03.790 --> 00:15:05.620
The girls won't leave me alone...

00:15:05.620 --> 00:15:06.750
Is that a brag?!

00:15:10.450 --> 00:15:11.460
This must be the place.

00:15:11.790 --> 00:15:14.580
Wow, it seems popular,
despite the remote location.

00:15:14.580 --> 00:15:16.250
Welcome!

00:15:16.250 --> 00:15:18.790
What...?! Takayashiki?!

00:15:18.790 --> 00:15:21.930
Hey, Tanoue-kun! Yoshioka-kun!
Thanks for coming!

00:15:21.950 --> 00:15:24.620
What's with your outfit?!

00:15:24.620 --> 00:15:26.040
How do I look?

00:15:26.040 --> 00:15:28.910
Well, don't mind me. Great timing!

00:15:28.910 --> 00:15:30.830
Come on in! Here!

00:15:32.540 --> 00:15:34.410
Thank you for waiting...

00:15:34.410 --> 00:15:37.870
Let me explain the game to you.

00:15:37.870 --> 00:15:39.500
Yes, head maid!

00:15:39.500 --> 00:15:42.830
This is impressive! What a crowd!

00:15:42.830 --> 00:15:46.870
We were completely empty just a while ago,
but it's thanks to this.

00:15:47.960 --> 00:15:50.920
What's this? And this girl...

00:15:51.290 --> 00:15:54.880
That's the cute transfer student
who's popular with the guys!

00:15:54.880 --> 00:15:59.040
Emmy told us about the school SNS!

00:15:59.040 --> 00:16:00.450
Emmy?

00:16:00.450 --> 00:16:02.330
See, over there.

00:16:02.330 --> 00:16:05.330
Thanks for waiting! Let's play a game!

00:16:05.330 --> 00:16:09.080
I see, she's the one the
male customers are here for.

00:16:09.080 --> 00:16:09.910
Tanoue-kun!

00:16:09.910 --> 00:16:10.810
Hmm?

00:16:10.980 --> 00:16:12.250
Take this, please!

00:16:12.250 --> 00:16:12.820
Huh?

00:16:12.820 --> 00:16:14.750
Manage this table for us, please!

00:16:14.750 --> 00:16:18.200
Manage?! You want me to explain this game?!

00:16:18.200 --> 00:16:21.500
Please! We're so hugely short-staffed!

00:16:21.500 --> 00:16:23.830
You're my only hope!

00:16:23.830 --> 00:16:26.750
G-Got it! You can count on me!

00:16:26.750 --> 00:16:28.790
Thank you so much!

00:16:28.790 --> 00:16:31.330
Heh, her only hope...

00:16:31.330 --> 00:16:33.250
Who's this guy?

00:16:33.250 --> 00:16:35.460
A dude? Seriously? That sucks.

00:16:37.120 --> 00:16:39.160
Come on, three!

00:16:37.120 --> 00:16:39.160
Oh, no, a one!

00:16:39.160 --> 00:16:41.620
What do I do here?

00:16:39.160 --> 00:16:41.620
This one is played here.

00:16:41.620 --> 00:16:42.910
I found a match!

00:16:41.620 --> 00:16:42.910
I don't have any!

00:16:42.910 --> 00:16:43.760
Got it! Goal!

00:16:42.910 --> 00:16:43.760
I don't have any!

00:16:44.330 --> 00:16:46.080
Customers out the door?!

00:16:46.080 --> 00:16:49.750
Awesome! This could be the most
popular place in the entire festival!

00:16:49.750 --> 00:16:55.120
You're right. Chairperson, your idea
to use the SNS to share information

00:16:55.120 --> 00:16:56.580
is a huge success.

00:16:56.580 --> 00:16:58.660
That's not the only thing.

00:16:58.660 --> 00:17:03.290
This is the work of those four girls,
and the power of board games.

00:17:03.290 --> 00:17:07.160
See, Shibusawa?
I was right about them, wasn't I?

00:17:10.620 --> 00:17:14.790
Look, a customer seems bored. Go say something.

00:17:14.790 --> 00:17:16.580
Huh? But... I...

00:17:16.580 --> 00:17:18.200
Excuse us!

00:17:19.290 --> 00:17:21.700
Can we get a game going over here please?

00:17:21.700 --> 00:17:23.410
Wait, Chairperson? We still have to...

00:17:23.410 --> 00:17:26.200
Relax, this is part of our job!

00:17:26.200 --> 00:17:27.540
Chairperson...

00:17:27.540 --> 00:17:29.330
Vice-Chair, too...

00:17:29.330 --> 00:17:31.330
Miki, take care of them all please!

00:17:31.330 --> 00:17:33.870
Oh... um...

00:17:33.870 --> 00:17:35.650
Yoshioka-kun!

00:17:36.620 --> 00:17:40.500
Would you like to play this game with us?

00:17:40.500 --> 00:17:44.040
Oh, um... I suppose I could.

00:17:44.040 --> 00:17:45.790
Please show me.

00:17:48.500 --> 00:17:52.450
Okay... Let me explain the game.

00:17:52.450 --> 00:17:55.870
This is a French card game called <i>Dobble</i> .

00:17:55.870 --> 00:17:59.370
Please take a look at these two cards.

00:17:59.370 --> 00:18:04.950
These two cards share just one symbol.
Can you tell which one?

00:18:07.290 --> 00:18:08.370
The clover.

00:18:08.370 --> 00:18:11.160
Correct. How about this one?

00:18:12.790 --> 00:18:14.540
Oh, the purple cat!

00:18:14.540 --> 00:18:19.040
Yes, correct. There are 55 cards in this game.

00:18:19.040 --> 00:18:23.870
If you take any two cards,
they always share just one symbol.

00:18:23.870 --> 00:18:26.660
What? Always one pair only?

00:18:26.660 --> 00:18:28.000
Really?

00:18:28.000 --> 00:18:29.290
Wow, she's right!

00:18:29.290 --> 00:18:31.200
That's kind of awesome.

00:18:31.200 --> 00:18:36.450
The goal in <i>Dobble</i> is to find the
common symbol faster than the others.

00:18:36.450 --> 00:18:40.450
The cards can be used to
play five different games.

00:18:40.450 --> 00:18:45.410
Today, we will play the
game called <i>Hot Potato</i> .

00:18:45.410 --> 00:18:52.160
First, play your card facedown like this.
On "go," turn it faceup.

00:18:52.160 --> 00:18:56.500
If you find a symbol on your card that
is the same on another person's card--

00:18:56.500 --> 00:19:04.290
"Cat"--say the name of the symbol
and force the card on that player.

00:19:04.290 --> 00:19:07.830
The last person to have
cards in their hand loses.

00:19:07.830 --> 00:19:10.000
A game of speed! Exciting!

00:19:10.000 --> 00:19:12.290
Sounds like fun! Let's play!

00:19:12.290 --> 00:19:14.790
Okay, I will deal the cards now.

00:19:16.620 --> 00:19:18.580
Is this really fun...?

00:19:19.580 --> 00:19:22.620
Okay, we'll start. Ready, go!

00:19:24.700 --> 00:19:25.750
Droplet!

00:19:24.700 --> 00:19:25.750
Key!

00:19:25.750 --> 00:19:27.300
Stop sign!

00:19:25.750 --> 00:19:27.300
Bomb!

00:19:27.300 --> 00:19:29.010
Next, ready, go!

00:19:30.330 --> 00:19:31.160
Bomb!

00:19:30.330 --> 00:19:31.160
Chess piece!

00:19:31.160 --> 00:19:32.310
Target!

00:19:32.540 --> 00:19:33.790
Impressive.

00:19:33.790 --> 00:19:36.310
You have great reflexes, Yoshioka-kun.

00:19:36.830 --> 00:19:39.830
I do kendo, so...

00:19:41.160 --> 00:19:43.690
Moving on, once more. Ready, go!

00:19:45.000 --> 00:19:45.830
Drop...

00:19:45.000 --> 00:19:45.830
Tear!

00:19:45.830 --> 00:19:46.330
Huh?!

00:19:45.830 --> 00:19:46.870
Light bulb!

00:19:46.330 --> 00:19:46.870
Sunglasses!

00:19:46.870 --> 00:19:47.570
Anchor!

00:19:48.750 --> 00:19:50.120
Wait, hold up!

00:19:50.120 --> 00:19:51.330
Huh?

00:19:51.330 --> 00:19:54.910
Is this a "tear"? Shouldn't it be a "droplet"?

00:19:54.910 --> 00:19:57.830
Oh, you're allowed to make up any name you want,

00:19:57.830 --> 00:20:00.870
as long as the other person gets it.

00:20:00.870 --> 00:20:05.330
Huh? Oh... Okay. Understood.

00:20:06.370 --> 00:20:09.130
Is it really okay to be so vague...?

00:20:09.950 --> 00:20:11.850
Now that I look at it,
a lot of the things are weird-looking...

00:20:12.350 --> 00:20:14.450
Alright, here we go!

00:20:14.450 --> 00:20:15.430
Ready, go!

00:20:17.100 --> 00:20:19.790
I found it! But what is this thing?

00:20:17.890 --> 00:20:18.560
Cheese!

00:20:19.790 --> 00:20:21.400
I have to think of something quick...

00:20:19.790 --> 00:20:21.400
Um... Black and white mark!

00:20:21.870 --> 00:20:25.150
You're allowed to make up any name you want.

00:20:25.150 --> 00:20:25.940
Got it!

00:20:26.580 --> 00:20:27.820
Smiley urchin!

00:20:29.790 --> 00:20:31.790
Smiley... urchin?

00:20:35.830 --> 00:20:37.660
Oh, this thing...?

00:20:37.660 --> 00:20:41.580
Smiley urchin? Oh, I get it.

00:20:41.580 --> 00:20:43.700
Wow, that's crazy!

00:20:43.700 --> 00:20:46.000
Um... Huh...?

00:20:46.000 --> 00:20:46.870
It's okay.

00:20:46.870 --> 00:20:48.000
Huh?

00:20:48.000 --> 00:20:50.790
That's the right way to do it, Yoshioka-kun.

00:20:54.700 --> 00:20:56.620
The festival was awesome!

00:20:56.620 --> 00:20:58.330
I know, right? Right?

00:20:58.330 --> 00:21:02.290
Look, everyone's had so much fun.

00:21:02.290 --> 00:21:06.700
This sucks. The chairperson
is always right in the end.

00:21:06.700 --> 00:21:10.040
Hmm? What's wrong, you look glum.

00:21:12.410 --> 00:21:17.120
If what you did was wrong, we wouldn't
get so many smiles from everyone.

00:21:17.120 --> 00:21:20.830
It's your hard work that got
them to smile so much.

00:21:22.540 --> 00:21:24.200
But...

00:21:25.250 --> 00:21:27.830
Obviously! No need to state the obvious!

00:21:28.870 --> 00:21:30.670
There it is! That's the Shibusawa Ren I know!

00:21:35.390 --> 00:21:37.290
So much fun!

00:21:37.290 --> 00:21:38.850
Let us play again sometime!

00:21:39.250 --> 00:21:41.290
Thanks for coming!

00:21:45.250 --> 00:21:47.080
It's over!

00:21:47.080 --> 00:21:48.500
I'm spent...

00:21:48.500 --> 00:21:50.030
That was tough...

00:21:51.910 --> 00:21:56.160
My first festival in high school,
thanks to board games,

00:21:53.120 --> 00:21:54.870
Good work, everyone!

00:21:54.870 --> 00:21:56.160
Going to the after party?

00:21:56.160 --> 00:21:58.700
There's like dancing in pairs and stuff, right?

00:21:56.160 --> 00:21:58.540
was a lot of work, but a huge amount of fun!

00:21:58.700 --> 00:21:59.330
What?!

00:21:59.330 --> 00:22:01.540
With the addition of a new friend,

00:21:59.740 --> 00:22:01.540
Let's go! Let's go!

00:22:01.910 --> 00:22:05.710
my world grew just a little bit bigger.

00:23:38.040 --> 00:23:42.060
I want to find out about
what Japanese children do to play!

00:23:42.660 --> 00:23:46.270
How does this game end, though?
